{"step_index":224,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:14:37Z","content":"I have completed the extension of the **StreamWave Serverless Media Platform** to include an original public landing page, simulated subscription checkout, signed HTTP-only cookie session management, and member access control.\n\n---\n\n### 📂 Files Changed & Created\n\n1. **[`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py)**:\n   - Added central `SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN` configuration (`StreamWave Monthly` - `US$2.99 per month`).\n   - Implemented HMAC-SHA256 session token creation and verification (`DEMO_SESSION_SECRET`).\n   - Created reusable FastAPI dependency `verify_paid_session` protecting `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events` (HTTP 401 Unauthorized for unpaid requests).\n   - Added API endpoints: `GET /api/session`, `POST /api/demo-payment`, `POST /api/logout`, and `POST /api/reset-demo`.\n   - Served HTML routes for `/`, `/checkout`, and `/library`.\n2. **[`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/index.html)**:\n   - Created the public landing page featuring the main copy:\n     - Heading: *\"Zimbabwe’s stories, music and movies — all in one place.\"*\n     - Supporting text: *\"Stream from US$2.99 per month. Cancel anytime.\"*\n     - Instruction: *\"Enter your email address to start your StreamWave membership.\"*\n   - Includes StreamWave logo, \"Sign In\" button, email field + **`Get Started ›`** action button, **Why Join StreamWave?** benefits grid, **How It Works** steps, **Supported Payment Methods** badges, and academic footer.\n3. **[`public/checkout.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/checkout.html)**:\n   - Created the academic checkout page featuring the prominent alert banner: *\"ACADEMIC PAYMENT SIMULATION — No real money will be charged. Do not enter genuine payment information.\"*\n   - Supports 3 simulated payment tabs:\n     - **EcoCash**: Prefilled test mobile number `077 000 0000`, 3-step visual simulation (*Sending push request...* -> *Waiting for PIN...* -> *Approved*).\n     - **Visa**: Masked test card `•••• •••• •••• 4242`.\n     - **MasterCard**: Masked test card `•••• •••• •••• 4444`.\n   - Sends ONLY `email`, `method`, and `plan_id` to `POST /api/demo-payment`. Never collects or logs financial credentials.\n4. **[`public/library.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/library.html)**:\n   - Created the protected member catalogue page displaying customer email (*Member: user@example.co.zw*), **Sign Out** button, and **Reset Demo** assessment control.\n   - Contains full catalogue grid, search bar, filters, audio player bar for music, and 5-second MP4 movie preview modal.\n5. **[`public/css/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/css/styles.css)** & **[`public/js/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/js/app.js)**:\n   - Added styles for landing hero, step cards, test card previews, progress animation, and member nav controls.\n   - Updated client app logic for `/library` session verification, protected API calls, and sign-out handling.\n6. **[`tests/test_api.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/tests/test_api.py)**:\n   - Created a 20-test automated unit test suite covering public routes, 401 access protection, checkout simulation, session cookies, sign out, and regression testing.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Endpoints Summary\n\n- **`GET /`**: Public landing page.\n- **`GET /checkout`**: Public simulated checkout page.\n- **`GET /library`**: Protected member catalogue library page.\n- **`GET /api/session`**: Public session status endpoint.\n- **`POST /api/demo-payment`**: Accepts `ecocash`, `visa`, or `mastercard` and sets signed `streamwave_session` HTTP-only cookie.\n- **`POST /api/logout`**: Clears session cookie and logs out.\n- **`POST /api/reset-demo`**: Assessment reset control endpoint.\n- **`GET /api/media`**, **`GET /api/media/{media_id}`**, **`POST /api/play-events`**: Protected catalogue APIs (requires signed session cookie).\n- **`GET /api/health`**, **`GET /docs`**, **`GET /redoc`**: Public system status and API documentation.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Test Verification & Coverage\n\nThe automated test suite in [`tests/test_api.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/tests/test_api.py) covers:\n- Public landing page (`/`) accessibility.\n- Public checkout page (`/checkout`) accessibility.\n- Unpaid user rejection on `/api/media` (HTTP 401).\n- Payment validation errors (invalid email/method -> HTTP 422).\n- EcoCash, Visa, and MasterCard simulation setting signed cookie.\n- Paid member access to `/api/media`, `/api/media/1`, and `/api/play-events`.\n- Sign out clearing session cookie.\n- 100% regression verification of catalogue search, filtering, music playback, and 5-second movie previews.\n\nTo run the test suite locally in Command Prompt (`cmd.exe`):\n```cmd\n.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pytest tests\\test_api.py -v\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Remaining Limitations\n1. **Academic Demonstration Payment**: No actual financial transaction processing or banking authorization occurs.\n2. **Public Static Sample Media Assets**: Media files (`/media/demo.wav` and `/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`) are served directly as static assets. Production deployment would require private object storage with signed URL delivery and Digital Rights Management (DRM) licensing."}
{"step_index":225,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:19:12Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nReview and refine the StreamWave landing page and simulated checkout created in the previous step.\r\n\r\nDo not change the working FastAPI architecture or payment-session logic unless necessary to fix a verified problem.\r\n\r\nLANDING-PAGE DESIGN\r\n\r\n1. Create a full-height hero section with a dark collage made only from the project’s existing or authorised StreamWave artwork.\r\n2. Position the StreamWave logo clearly in the header.\r\n3. Add a restrained “Sign In” button on the right.\r\n4. Centre the main heading, supporting copy, email field and “Get Started” button.\r\n5. Ensure the call-to-action remains visible without excessive scrolling on common desktop screens.\r\n6. Add a dark overlay so text remains readable.\r\n7. Do not copy Netflix’s logo, content, exact wording or proprietary artwork.\r\n8. Preserve StreamWave’s red, white and graphite visual identity.\r\n\r\nCHECKOUT EXPERIENCE\r\n\r\n1. Present EcoCash, Visa and MasterCard as three clear selectable options.\r\n2. Display the selected method’s demonstration steps only after selection.\r\n3. Include processing, approved and declined demonstration states.\r\n4. Provide an explicit “Simulate Successful Payment” button.\r\n5. Provide a smaller “Test Declined Payment” option for technical demonstration.\r\n6. Disable repeated submissions while processing.\r\n7. Display the generated demonstration transaction reference on success.\r\n8. Redirect to `/library` only after the approved backend response.\r\n9. Never request or store real payment credentials.\r\n\r\nACCESSIBILITY AND RESPONSIVENESS\r\n\r\n* Ensure correct semantic headings and labels.\r\n* Add visible keyboard-focus states.\r\n* Support Escape where modal dialogs are used.\r\n* Make payment choices keyboard accessible.\r\n* Provide screen-reader status messages during processing.\r\n* Respect reduced-motion settings.\r\n* Test desktop, tablet and mobile layouts.\r\n* Prevent horizontal scrolling.\r\n* Ensure the hero, checkout and library work at small-screen widths.\r\n\r\nVerify the complete visitor journey:\r\n\r\nLanding page → Email validation → Checkout → Select payment method → Simulated approval → Paid session → Library → Play movie preview or music sample → Sign out.\r\n\r\nFix all problems and report the actual checks completed.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T21:19:12+02:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":226,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:19:13Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Landing Page Design**\n\nI'm currently focused on the landing page's design, specifically the hero section. I'm exploring the implications of a full-height or near full-height hero section with a dark collage background. I need to consider how this visual choice impacts overall user engagement and initial impressions. I'm thinking about how the background will make the site accessible, and its implications on the usability of the site.\n\n\n**Refining the Landing Page**\n\nI've been refining the landing page, and focusing in on accessibility and design. The StreamWave branding is front and center. I'm ensuring the header features the logo and a restrained \"Sign In\" button, and the centered hero content includes the main heading, supporting copy, an email field, and a \"Get Started\" button. I'm also ensuring the call-to-action remains visible without excessive scrolling. I'm using a dark overlay to maintain text readability and utilizing the StreamWave's brand colors.\n\n\n**Implementing Payment Decline Logic**\n\nI'm now implementing the backend support for simulating payment declines in `app.py`. I'm updating the `POST /api/demo-payment` endpoint to accept a simulation flag. When this flag is set, I'll log a decline event, and return a 400 or 402 status code to simulate the decline. I'm also ensuring that no session cookie is issued for declined payments to mirror real-world behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation Plan for refining StreamWave landing page, checkout experience with success/decline simulation, accessibility, and full visitor journey verification.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Implementation Plan - Refined Landing Page, Checkout & Accessibility\n\nRefine and polish the **StreamWave Entertainment** platform with a full-height landing hero section, enhanced checkout simulation (including explicit decline demonstration and transaction reference displays), complete accessibility features (keyboard focus, screen reader live region status), and full mobile/desktop responsiveness.\n\n---\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Simulated Payment States**: The checkout page will now include two explicit action buttons:\n> 1. **Simulate Successful Payment** (Primary Red Button) -> Approves payment, generates `SW-DEMO-XXXXX` transaction reference, sets session cookie, and redirects to `/library`.\n> 2. **Test Declined Payment** (Secondary Link/Button) -> Demonstrates a simulated payment decline (card/mobile issuer rejection) without setting a cookie or granting library access.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Accessibility Improvements**: Adds ARIA live regions (`aria-live=\"polite\"`), explicit focus visible indicators (`:focus-visible`), keyboard support for payment tabs, Escape key modal closing, and `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` support.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Backend Refinements\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py)\n- Update `DemoPaymentRequest` model:\n  ```python\n  class DemoPaymentRequest(BaseModel):\n      email: str\n      method: str\n      plan_id: Optional[str] = \"streamwave-monthly\"\n      simulate_decline: Optional[bool] = False\n  ```\n- In `POST /api/demo-payment`:\n  - If `simulate_decline=True`: log structured JSON event (`\"status\": \"declined\"`), return HTTP 400 with detail: `\"Simulated payment decline: Card or mobile issuer rejected transaction.\"` without setting session cookie.\n\n---\n\n### Landing Page Refinements\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/index.html)\n- Full-height hero section (`min-height: 92vh`) centered in viewport.\n- StreamWave logo on left, restrained \"Sign In\" button on right.\n- Centered main heading, supporting text, email field, and **Get Started ›** button.\n- Dark collage artwork backdrop with high-contrast gradient overlay.\n- Accessible form labels and ARIA live feedback.\n\n---\n\n### Checkout Refinements\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/checkout.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/checkout.html)\n- Display selected payment method steps only after selection.\n- Add explicit action buttons:\n  - **Simulate Successful Payment** (Primary button)\n  - **Test Declined Payment** (Secondary outline button)\n- Disable submission buttons while processing to prevent duplicate requests.\n- ARIA live region (`role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"`) announcing progress steps to screen readers.\n- On success: display generated transaction reference (`SW-DEMO-XXXXX`) in a success state container before redirecting to `/library`.\n- On decline: display a clear error state box with retry button.\n\n---\n\n### Styles & Accessibility\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/css/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/css/styles.css)\n- Full-height hero layout (`min-height: 92vh`, flexbox centering).\n- Explicit high-contrast `:focus-visible` outline (`outline: 2px solid #e50914`).\n- `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` rules disabling progress animations.\n- Ensure strict `overflow-x: hidden` to prevent horizontal scrolling on small screens.\n\n---\n\n### Test Suite Updates\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`tests/test_api.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/tests/test_api.py)\n- Add test case verifying simulated payment decline (`simulate_decline=True`) returns HTTP 400 and does NOT set a session cookie.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Tests\nRun pytest in Windows Command Prompt:\n```cmd\n.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pytest tests\\test_api.py -v\n```\n\n### Manual Visitor Journey Verification\n1. **Landing Page (`/`)**: Verify full-height hero, logo placement, email entry, and **Get Started ›** click.\n2. **Checkout Page (`/checkout`)**:\n   - Test EcoCash, Visa, MasterCard tab selections.\n   - Click **Test Declined Payment** -> Observe processing animation -> Displays decline state.\n   - Click **Simulate Successful Payment** -> Observe processing steps -> Displays `SW-DEMO-XXXXX` transaction ref -> Redirects to `/library`.\n3. **Library (`/library`)**:\n   - Verify member status bar.\n   - Play 5-second movie preview and music sample.\n   - Click **Sign Out** -> Confirms cookie cleared and redirects to `/`.\n","Description":"Create implementation plan for refining landing page, checkout, accessibility, and decline simulation","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Creating implementation plan","toolSummary":"Creating implementation plan"}}]}
